{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-221326-r4524784","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Hummus with Sprouted Chickpea","sourcePageId":221326,"sourceRevision":"4524784","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-07-17T23:45:41Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Hummus%20with%20Sprouted%20Chickpea&oldid=4524784","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T13:05:28.092Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Appetizer recipes","Category:Easy recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes for dip","Category:Recipes for hummus","Category:Recipes using agave","Category:Recipes using chickpea","Category:Recipes using ground cumin","Category:Recipes using lemon"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"45d538b34e498018a5574a57148306990122a1f8b802c4c54bbc78345c9b172b","sourceWikitext":"__NOTOC__\n{{recipesummary|category=Appetizer recipes|servings=6|time=1 hour|difficulty=2}}\n\n{{recipe}} | [[Cookbook:Appetizers|Appetizers]]]\n\nHummus is a classic dish likely originating from mid-eastern cultures. This recipe incorporates entirely raw ingredients for a truly healthy, delicious taste. \n\n==Ingredients==\n\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Cup|cups]] [[Cookbook:Chickpea|chickpeas]]\n* ⅓ cup [[Cookbook:Sesame Seed|sesame seeds]]\n* 3 cloves [[Cookbook:Garlic|garlic]]\n* ¼ white [[Cookbook:Onion|onion]]\n* 1 peeled [[Cookbook:Lemon|lemon]]\n* ⅓ cup sun-dried [[Cookbook:Tomato|tomato]]\n* 5 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tablespoons]] [[Cookbook:Agave Syrup|agave syrup]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|teaspoon]] [[Cookbook:Salt|salt]]\n* 3 tablespoons ground [[Cookbook:Cumin|cumin]]\n* 3 tablespoons fresh [[Cookbook:Parsley|parsley]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Pinch|pinch]] [[Cookbook:Paprika|paprika]]\n* 2 tablespoons [[Cookbook:Olive Oil|olive oil]]\n\n==Procedure==\n\n# Soak chickpeas for 12–24 hours then let sprout for 1–2 days. Make sure to rinse three times a day while sprouting.\n# Combine all ingredients except olive oil, paprika, and fresh parsley in a [[Cookbook:Blender|blender]] or [[Cookbook:Food Processor|food processor]], and [[Cookbook:Puréeing|purée]] until smooth. Refrigerate for best taste.\n# Sprinkle hummus with olive oil, paprika, and parsley when serving.\n\n==Notes, tips, and variations==\n\n* For a spicy taste you may add roasted red [[Cookbook:Chiles|chili pepper]] or a dash of [[Cookbook:Cayenne Pepper|cayenne pepper]].\n* Adding fresh parsley and paprika along with drizzling olive oil over the hummus really takes it over the top.\n* You may serve with pita bread for dipping. Chips or fresh vegetables compliment nicely as well.\n\n[[Category:Recipes using chickpea]]\n[[Category:Recipes using ground cumin]]\n[[Category:Appetizer recipes|{{PAGENAME}}]]\n[[Category:Recipes for dip|{{PAGENAME}}]]\n[[Category:Recipes using agave]]\n[[Category:Recipes for hummus]]\n[[Category:Recipes using lemon]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Hummus with Sprouted Chickpea","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"2 cups chickpeas","sourceText":"2 cups chickpeas","amountText":"2 cups chickpeas","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"⅓ cup sesame seeds","sourceText":"⅓ cup sesame seeds","amountText":"⅓ cup sesame seeds","amount":null,